{"id":115901,"title":"Hybrid Parallelism for Volume Rendering on Large, Multi-core Systems","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=scientific volume visualization","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/m2/1/high_res_d/994007.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"fe0313e23ecb524f5b43b4ee2fbf8fedce7c21b6f2fe7953c8efdc33d4ebd300","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793236829.5131176,"text_chars":21144,"abstract":"This work studies the performance and scalability characteristics of\"hybrid\" parallel programming and execution as applied to raycasting volume rendering -- a staple visualization algorithm -- on a large, multi-core platform. Historically, the Message Passing Interface (MPI) has become the de-facto standard for parallel programming and execution on modern parallel systems. As the computing industry trends towards multi-core processors, with four- and six-core chips common today and 128-core chips coming soon, we wish to better understand how algorithmic and parallel programming choices impact performance and scalability on large, distributed-memory multi-core systems. Our findings indicate that the hybrid-parallel implementation, at levels of concurrency ranging from 1,728 to 216,000, performs better, uses a smaller absolute memory footprint, and consumes less communication bandwidth than the traditional, MPI-only implementation.","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/m2/1/high_res_d/994007.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=scientific volume visualization","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=distributed volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=parallel volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=volume rendering library","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=volume rendering data parallelism","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=cpu ray casting volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=fixed step volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=distributed shared virtual memory volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=pixel ray image volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=distributed parallel volume ray-casting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=load imbalance volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=volume ray casting algorithm","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=interval integration volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=intra-ray parallelism volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=levoy volume ray casting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=hybrid ray casting volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=parallel direct compositing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=parallel volume ray casting library","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=parallel image compositing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=front-to-back volume raycasting","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc1014428/?q=distributed ray casting mpi"],"cited_by":[{"path":"12235-radix-k-compositing.md","name":"Radix-k Compositing","k":2},{"path":"21181-hybrid-parallel-volume-rendering.md","name":"Hybrid Parallel Volume Rendering","k":3},{"path":"20911-mpi-hybrid-compositing.md","name":"MPI-hybrid Compositing","k":2},{"path":"20922-mpi-hybrid-raycasting.md","name":"MPI-hybrid Raycasting","k":2}]}